---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Roadmap — Tempo"
  description="What's coming next for Tempo. V1.x focus — no dates committed, the list updates as features ship."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>Roadmap</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      What's coming next for Tempo. Focus is on V1.x — improving the core
      experience, growing the score catalog, opening new bridges into the
      Mac. No dates. The list updates as features ship.
    </p>
    <p class="lede-secondary">
      Items are grouped by release window (V1.1, V1.2, V1.3, V1.4) and then
      a continuous "later" pool. The ordering inside each window is a
      working plan, not a contract; bugs and user requests jump the queue
      every release.
    </p>
  </header>

  <main class="doc">

    <section class="group">
      <h2>V1.1</h2>
      <ul class="items">
        <li>
          <strong>Apple Shortcuts integration</strong> <em>(any genre, every tempo)</em> —
          a <code>SendEventToTempoIntent</code> App Intent, Spotlight quick-entry
          via AppShortcuts, plus a handful of demo <code>.shortcut</code> files
          covering Mail rules, voice memos, Focus modes, SSH health checks,
          generic URL endpoints, Wake-on-LAN, and an iOS geofence bonus.
          AppleScript snippets for DEVONthink and OmniFocus on the side.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Timeline filtering</strong> — a quick toggle to switch
          between <em>all events</em> and <em>only those needing attention</em>.
          Sits in the toolbar, persists across launches, composes with search
          (AND), orthogonal to source hide.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Conditional action visibility</strong> — when an action's
          template (<code>${'$'}{'{metadata.X}'}</code>) doesn't resolve, the button
          hides instead of showing greyed-out with a warning triangle. Cleaner
          panels without manual score edits.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Demo mode</strong> — an in-app toggle that seeds a sample
          timeline so new users can try the UI before wiring up real sources.
          Includes a persistent banner so it's never confused with the real
          feed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Todoist score</strong> — pulled forward from the continuous
          pool. Tasks, comments, completions surfaced on the timeline next to
          everything else.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="group">
      <h2>V1.2</h2>
      <ul class="items">
        <li>
          <strong>Sorting toggle (by severity)</strong> — companion to the
          filtering toggle. Toolbar UI is shared; day headers fold away when
          the view isn't chronological.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Sound customization</strong> — drop-in folder for your own
          alert sounds, sitting alongside the bundled set.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Map preview inline</strong> for Calendar events with a
          location — rendered via <code>MKMapSnapshotter</code> as a thumbnail
          on the event row, same pattern as Protect snapshots.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="group">
      <h2>V1.3</h2>
      <ul class="items">
        <li>
          <strong>Proxmox native adapter</strong> — a first-class ingestion
          endpoint for Proxmox VE webhooks (PVE 8.1+), in addition to the
          downloadable score.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Source liveness detection</strong> — base implementation.
          Each source declares an expected liveness window; Tempo flags the
          source as silent when it's been quiet past its threshold (you've
          seen the orange dot on Synology already — this generalises it).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Action quality cluster</strong> — label interpolation
          (e.g. <code>"Copy ${'$'}{'{metadata.ip}'}"</code> renders the value
          on the button), multi-segment <code>copyToClipboard</code>, a new
          <code>revealInFinder</code> action trigger, and visual section
          dividers in long action panels.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Time Machine — built-in provider</strong> — listens to
          <code>com.apple.backupd</code> notifications so Time Machine
          successes/failures land on the timeline like any other event,
          without any user setup.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="group">
      <h2>V1.4</h2>
      <ul class="items">
        <li>
          <strong>In-app score browser</strong> — install scores from
          inside Tempo, browse the catalog with search and filters, manage
          versions, no more browser hop to GitHub.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Heatmap temporal markers</strong> — month labels, weekend
          tinting, and month-boundary dividers in the historical heatmap.
          Patterns over a quarter become readable at a glance.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="group">
      <h2>V1.5 and later, continuous</h2>
      <p>
        Items below ship as they're ready, without a fixed release-window
        commitment. Sequencing is driven by community feedback after
        launch.
      </p>
      <ul class="items">
        <li>
          <strong>Score catalog growth</strong> — Stripe / Paddle, GitHub
          (Issues / PRs / Discussions / Mentions), RSS via script, extended
          Todoist patterns, and continuous additions in the homelab,
          self-hosted, media, and Mac power-user clusters listed on the
          <a href="/gallery/">gallery</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>External archive</strong> — per-source archive file with
          a schema that adapts to the payload, so events can be retained
          indefinitely outside the working DB without losing structure.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>User-requested features</strong> — driven by Discord
          beta feedback and GitHub Issues after launch. Some of these will
          jump ahead of items listed above; that's the point.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bug fixes and community-response polish</strong> — a
          mandatory slot in every release. The list of "what's currently
          rough" is a moving target by design.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="group parking">
      <h2>Parking lot</h2>
      <p>
        Items that need an external trigger before they're picked up.
        Listed here for transparency; ask in the community if any of these
        block your use case.
      </p>
      <ul class="items">
        <li>
          <strong>Obsidian score</strong> — needs an Obsidian plugin
          contributor (TypeScript). Outreach to <code>r/ObsidianMD</code> is
          planned after V1.1 ships.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Thumbnail click-to-zoom + full-resolution storage</strong> —
          conditional on community demand. Use case: 1–8-camera homelab
          forensic inspection. Power-users with 50+ cameras are enterprise
          NVR territory, not Tempo.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="group">
      <h2>Beyond V1</h2>
      <p>
        V2 plans aren't published. They'll come into focus once V1 has a
        few months of community use behind it — that feedback is what shapes
        the V2 pitch, so committing now would be premature.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="group">
      <h2>Want to influence this?</h2>
      <p>
        Open an issue, drop a note on the
        <a href="/community/">Discord</a>, or email
        <a href="mailto:hello@tempoapp.app">hello@tempoapp.app</a>. The
        roadmap above is a working plan, not a fence — concrete, well-argued
        requests change it.
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>

  <style>
    .page-header {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 48px auto 24px;
      padding: 0 24px;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .page-header h1 {
      font-size: 36px;
      margin: 0 0 16px;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .lede {
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 1.65;
      color: var(--text);
      padding: 16px 20px;
      background: var(--bg2);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }
    .lede-secondary {
      color: var(--text2);
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      padding: 0 4px;
    }
    .doc {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 0 auto 80px;
      padding: 0 24px;
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      line-height: 1.65;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .doc .group {
      margin-top: 40px;
    }
    .doc .group.parking {
      opacity: 0.85;
    }
    .doc h2 {
      font-size: 22px;
      margin: 0 0 16px;
      color: var(--text);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .doc p {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      color: var(--text2);
    }
    .doc a {
      color: var(--blue);
    }
    .items {
      list-style: disc;
      padding-left: 1.4rem;
      color: var(--text2);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .items li {
      margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    }
    .items strong {
      color: var(--text);
      font-weight: 500;
    }
    .items em {
      color: var(--text3);
      font-style: italic;
    }
    .items code {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.88em;
      background: var(--bg2);
      padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
      border-radius: 4px;
      color: var(--text);
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
